// This code is for demonstration purposes only, showing how to perform data acquisition and FFT Calculation using the Teensy 4.1 ADC1 
// Code characteristics:
// - Data acquisition is performed via channel A0 of ADC1 of the Teensy 4.1.
// - A voltage sensor based on a differential amplifier will be connected to channel A0 (ADC1)
// - The acquisition sequence for ADC1 will consist of only 1 channel (A0). 
// - The ADC_ETC trigger will be generated by PIT Channel 0 at 4096.01 Hz. It is not possible to generate a frequency of exactly 4096 Hz using the PIT on the Teensy 4.1.
// - The PIT_TRIGGER0 (XBAR1_IN56) is routed to ADC_ETC_TRIG00 (XBAR1_OUT103) by XBAR
// - The FFT calculation will be performed via the CMSIS-DSP library (Cortex Microcontroller Software Interface Standard). 4096 voltage points will
//   be acquired at a rate of 4096.01 Hz, implying a frequency resolution of 1.0000024Hz. The Hann window function is applied to the signal before the FFT calculation,
//   using a function from the CMSIS-DSP library itself.
// 
// - IMPORTANT CONFIGURATION - Chech the parameters below in Arduino IDE Tools:
//       - Tools → Optimize → Fastest
//       - Tools → CPU Speed → 600 MHz
// Warning: Update the Arduino_CMSIS-DSP library in the Arduino IDE library manager.
//          See https://ernane-aac.github.io/Teensy-4.1--How-to-Configure-the-ADC-System/ for more details on ADC configuration on the Teensy 4.1.
//          See https://ernane-aac.github.io/Teensy-4.1-Sinusoidal-Pulse-Width-Modulation/ for more details on FlexPWM configuration on the Teensy 4.1.    
// ========================================================================================

